/**
 * FUNERAL WEBSITE FORMS BACKEND: Google Sheets database + Gmail alerts (free).
 * GENERATED by `npm run apps-script` from site/forms.mjs. Do not edit the FORMS section by hand.
 *
 * SETUP (about 10 minutes, signed in as the funeral home's Google account):
 *  1. Create a new Google Sheet (sheets.new) and name it "Website forms".
 *  2. In the Sheet: Extensions → Apps Script. Delete the sample code, paste ALL of this file, and click Save.
 *  3. In the function menu at the top choose  setup  and click Run. Allow the permissions it asks for.
 *     (Google warns because this is your own script: "Advanced" → "Go to … (unsafe)" → Allow.)
 *     This creates one tab per form, plus a daily clean-up job that deletes old data.
 *  4. Deploy → New deployment → gear icon → Web app.
 *       Execute as: Me    ·    Who has access: Anyone      → Deploy
 *  5. Copy the "Web app URL" (it ends in /exec) and put it in site/config.json as "formsEndpoint",
 *     or give it to Claude to add.
 *
 * DAILY USE
 *  - Each form has its own tab. Newest rows are at the bottom. Set "status" to contacted or closed as you work.
 *  - Condolences: change "status" from pending to approved to publish a message, or rejected to hide it.
 *  - Alerts go to ALERT_EMAIL. Urgent forms (a death, call-backs) are marked 🔴 URGENT.
 *
 * After changing this code: Deploy → Manage deployments → pencil icon → Version: New version → Deploy.
 * The URL stays the same.
 */
